kcov-marker-resync.patch -- a trace record that starts with the kcov
marker ends any open single-quote state (base#1415). Applied in the
kcov-builder stage of dockerfile/Dockerfile.test-tools AFTER
kcov-bash53-ansi-c.patch, on top of which it was generated. Only the diff
below is applied (`git apply` skips this header); if a KCOV_VERSION bump
moves its context, the apply fails and so does the build.

v43's checkEvents, while its quote state is SINGLE_QUOTE, feeds the next
line to getInputType and returns without parsing a marker. bash prints
the expanded operand of `[[ ]]` raw, so `_c="'"; [[ "${_c}" == '`' ]]`
traces as `kcov@FILE@LINENO@[[ ' == \` ]]`: one unescaped quote, state
left in SINGLE_QUOTE, and the following marker lines are dropped. The
diff makes a line that starts a marker record (k+cov@FILE@LINENO@, the
leading k repeats per subshell level) reset the state and parse as
normal. Continuation lines of a real multi-line value carry no marker and
stay swallowed. Trade-off: a continuation line that itself begins with a
`kcov@path@N@` marker would be read as a record.
Drop it when a kcov release carries an equivalent resync;
test/bats/unit/kcov_bash_instrumentation_spec.bats is the check.

diff --git a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
index 20b055b..65429b0 100644
--- a/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
+++ b/src/engines/bash-engine.cc
@@ -282,8 +282,12 @@ public:
 		// Line markers always start with kcov@
 
 		if (m_inputType == INPUT_SINGLE_QUOTE) {
-			m_inputType = getInputType(cur);
-			return true;
+			if (!startsWithMarker(cur)) {
+				m_inputType = getInputType(cur);
+				return true;
+			}
+			// A new marker record: the quote state belongs to the previous record.
+			m_inputType = INPUT_NORMAL;
 		}
 
 		size_t kcovStr = cur.find("kcov@");
@@ -540,6 +544,27 @@ private:
 		return out;
 	}
 
+	// True when str starts a trace record: k+cov@FILE@LINENO@ (bash repeats
+	// the first PS4 character once per subshell level).
+	static bool startsWithMarker(const std::string &str)
+	{
+		std::string::size_type i = 0;
+
+		while (i < str.size() && str[i] == 'k')
+			i++;
+		if (i == 0 || str.compare(i, 4, "cov@") != 0)
+			return false;
+		i += 4;
+		i = str.find('@', i);
+		if (i == std::string::npos)
+			return false;
+		i++;
+		std::string::size_type digits = i;
+		while (i < str.size() && str[i] >= '0' && str[i] <= '9')
+			i++;
+		return i > digits && i < str.size() && str[i] == '@';
+	}
+
 	enum InputType getInputType(const std::string &str)
 	{
 		enum InputType out = m_inputType;
